Module: Mathlib.Order.Booleanisation
Name: Booleanisation.LT
Description: The less-than relation on the Booleanization `Booleanisation α` is defined as follows for elements `a, b` of the generalized Boolean algebra `α`:
- For elements in `α`, `a < b` holds if and only if it holds in `α`.
- For an element `a` in `α` and a complement `bᶜ`, `a < bᶜ` holds if and only if `a` and `b` are disjoint in `α`.
- For complements `aᶜ` and `bᶜ`, `aᶜ < bᶜ` holds if and only if `b < a` holds in `α`.
- The relation `aᶜ < b` never holds for any `a, b` in `α`.
