Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Pi.Basic
Name: Sum.elim_mul_mul
Description: For any type $\gamma$ equipped with a multiplication operation, and for any functions $a, a' : \alpha \to \gamma$ and $b, b' : \beta \to \gamma$, the pointwise multiplication of the combined functions $\mathrm{Sum.elim}\,a\,b$ and $\mathrm{Sum.elim}\,a'\,b'$ is equal to the combined function of the pointwise multiplications $\mathrm{Sum.elim}\,(a * a')\,(b * b')$. In other words,
\[
\mathrm{Sum.elim}\,(a * a')\,(b * b') = (\mathrm{Sum.elim}\,a\,b) * (\mathrm{Sum.elim}\,a'\,b').
\]
