Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Group.UniqueProds.Basic
Name: UniqueMul.mulHom_image_iff
Description: Let $G$ and $H$ be multiplicative structures with $H$ having decidable equality, and let $f \colon G \to H$ be an injective multiplicative homomorphism. For any finite subsets $A, B \subseteq G$ and elements $a_0 \in A$, $b_0 \in B$, the following are equivalent:
1. The product $f(a_0) \cdot f(b_0)$ has a unique decomposition in $f(A) \times f(B)$ (i.e., $\text{UniqueMul}(f(A), f(B), f(a_0), f(b_0))$ holds)
2. The product $a_0 \cdot b_0$ has a unique decomposition in $A \times B$ (i.e., $\text{UniqueMul}(A, B, a_0, b_0)$ holds)
