1. [THEOREM] Denominator of $\frac{m}{n}$ is 1 iff $n \mid m$ for natural numbers
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Lemmas
Name: Rat.den_div_natCast_eq_one_iff
Description: For any natural numbers $m$ and $n$ with $n \neq 0$, the denominator of the rational number $\frac{m}{n}$ is equal to $1$ if and only if $n$ divides $m$.
Signature:  (m n : ℕ) (hn : n ≠ 0) : ((m : ℚ) / n).den = 1 ↔ n ∣ m

2. [THEOREM] Rational Number as Fraction of Its Numerator and Denominator
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs
Name: Rat.num_divInt_den
Description: For any rational number $q$, the fraction formed by its numerator $q.\text{num}$ and denominator $q.\text{den}$ (as integers) is equal to $q$ itself, i.e., $\frac{q.\text{num}}{q.\text{den}} = q$.
Signature:  (q : ℚ) : q.num /. q.den = q

3. [THEOREM] Characterization of Rational Numbers with Unit Denominator
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs
Name: Rat.den_eq_one_iff
Description: For any rational number $r$, the denominator of $r$ equals $1$ if and only if the canonical embedding of its numerator into the rational numbers equals $r$, i.e., $r.\text{den} = 1 \leftrightarrow r.\text{num} = r$.
Signature:  (r : ℚ) : r.den = 1 ↔ ↑r.num = r
