&= 4 ^{2^{m}} \cdot A \;+\; 6 ^{2^{m}} \cdot B \;+\; 9 ^{2^{m}} \cdot C .\tag{4}
\end{aligned}
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5.  Factor the common sum `f (2 ^ m)`.

Recall from `hfxm` that  

\[
f (2^{m}) = 4 ^{2^{m}} + 6 ^{2^{m}} + 9 ^{2^{m}} .\tag{5}
\]

Observe that the right–hand side of (4) can be written as the product of the
sum (5) with the *single* natural number  

\[
