### 6.  Conclude the existence of `k`.

Equation (6) defines a concrete natural number `k`.  
Equation (7) shows that this `k` satisfies the required equality.  Therefore

\[
\exists k,\; f (2^{n}) = f (2^{m}) \cdot k .
\]

